From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:29:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] LEAD_IN (off): the power/counter lead wraps on the kick he
 sees

A lead puller (not counter GH, which keeps its surface read) turns up
1.4 yd inside the kicked end's seen body, never outside the called hole,
re-read each decision beat from his own pictures of the installed kicker
and end; a log seen before his turn-up (kicker joined on the end's
outside) sends him around it. The kicker's private 'block-log' tag is not
read. Turned up, he takes the first unblocked second-level defender whose
seen motion shows in his lane, inside-out, met on the climbs' intercept
law, and fits him once he is within his own strike reach plus one
decision beat of their seen closing speed (not a fixed 1.2 yd).

The installed kick (kicker, end, called hole) is recorded on the lead's
plan at the snap. Default off; flag-off probe rows are byte-identical.
Contract test: test/lead-in.test.ts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
